  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p>The&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1011</mn><mi>th</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;term from the end in the binomial expansion of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2022</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1024</mn></math>&nbsp;times&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1011</mn><mi>th</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;term from the beginning,</p><p>So, according to question we have,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1013</mn></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1011</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1012</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>2022</mn></mmultiscripts><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>1010</mn></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mn>1012</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>1010</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>2022</mn></mmultiscripts><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>1012</mn></msup><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mn>1010</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msup><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>10</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>16</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>32</mn><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p>Note this question was bonus in Jee Main 2023 April session as answer key was not matching, so we have modified the question.</p>"
